Z||000000||GodSend||08-23-2001||04:34 PM||||Not 3 hours after I got new tires put on my 87 I found out that the center cap of one of my rims came off when I was driving (I know it was on when I left the shop).<P>I am not sure what type they are (although It did say something under the center caps.. so I will take a look tomorrow).  I am going to retrace my steps and see if I can find it on the road.... but Im not optimistic.  <P>Any idea how I can find a replacement? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-23-2001||05:01 PM||||first if you dont find it, go back to the dealer who mounted them and complain. If you have too just go where you got the rims and have them order a new center for you. Prob only a few bucks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||08-23-2001||05:48 PM||||Fiero store has them<BR>with Logo-$19 ea.--ouch<BR>plain $5 ea.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GodSend||08-23-2001||09:38 PM||||hrmm, seems like I need to do a little more explaining  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The rims came with the car when I bought it.  They seem to be some type of no-namers, but I can check on that.  I am actually missing the entire piece that covers the lugs. (An allan screw held this plate in place).  It is probably about 5 inchs in Diameter.<P>Is this piece standard to rims of this type (the hidden lug type).  I know the store will simply shrug their shoulders..... <P><BR>ugh!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||08-24-2001||12:37 AM||||I worked at a few tire stores, and this does happen every now and then...not usually a sign of poor work, it happens to the best of us sometimes.  The way to know if you're dealing with a good shop is simple; go back and tell them your centercap fell off on the way home and you can't find it anywhere.  If they're a good shop, they'll find someway to take care of the problem (centercaps as you've described are pretty generic...you can get four new ones that will most likely fit and the screws for probably 40 bucks their cost).  If it was a shotty place you were working with in the first place, they'll say they don't know what to say, and they can't help you.<P>If they help you, make sure to be very courteous, and thank them for being helpful and understanding <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  If they don't help you, you have a new opportunity to vent some pressure on somebody (I know you've been holding something in <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).  Some shops suck, some are great...it's the little things that make the difference.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
